  <title>Correspondence</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>General</gui><gui>Correspondence</gui></guiseq> lists the
  mail kept in the database, newest first. The <gui>Correspondence</gui>
  button of the <link xref="contact_hub"/>, and a double click on the
  <gui>Correspondence</gui> tab of <link xref="contact_history"/>, open it
  already showing one contact.</p>

  <p>The mail comes from three places:</p>
  <list>
    <item><p>Every message sent from PyGtk Posting, see <link
    xref="send_email"/>. It is filed under the contact it went to and, when
    it carried an invoice, under the invoice too.</p></item>
    <item><p>The folders ticked under <gui>Read folders</gui> in <link
    xref="settings#mail_accounts"/>, read from the mail server every five
    minutes.</p></item>
    <item><p>Old mail brought in with <link
    xref="mail_archive_import"/>.</p></item>
  </list>

  <section id="finding">
  <title>Finding a message</title>
  <terms>
    <item><title><gui>Contact</gui></title>
    <p>Shows only the mail filed under that contact. <gui>Clear</gui> shows
    everyone's mail again.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>From</gui> and <gui>to</gui></title>
    <p>The dates to show. The window opens on the last year. When nothing is
    found but older mail exists, the line at the bottom gives the date of the
    oldest message, so you know to widen the dates.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Both ways</gui>, <gui>Sent</gui>, <gui>Received</gui></title>
    <p>Which way the messages went. Mail in the account's Sent folder counts
    as sent.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Search the subject</gui></title>
    <p>Narrows the list to messages whose subject or contact contains what
    you type.</p></item>
  </terms>
  <p>The list updates itself when mail is sent or read from the server, on
  any computer. The <gui>Contact</gui> column shows the contacts a message is
  filed under, or the address it came from or went to when it is filed under
  none. <gui>Attached</gui> says whether it had attachments.</p>
  <note><p>Mail read from the server is not filed under a contact, so it is
  listed only while no contact is chosen.</p></note>
  </section>

  <section id="reading">
  <title>Reading a message</title>
  <p>Select a message to read it below the list. <gui>This message is
  about</gui> lists what it is filed under: its contacts, and the invoice
  when it carried one. Select the invoice and click <gui>Open</gui>, or
  double click it, to open its PDF. The PDF comes from the invoice itself, so
  it is the copy that was posted.</p>
  <p>Only the text of each message is kept, not its attachments, and mail
  read from the server or an archive keeps the first 64 KB of its text. The
  server still has the whole message.</p>
  <p><gui>Save window layout</gui>, in the window menu, remembers the
  window's size, where the list and the message divide, and the column
  widths, on this computer.</p>
  </section>

